RED on 6f3dc7c (5 failures, evidence/A6_red.txt), verified defects:

* parts.hostname strips the IPv6 brackets, so the rebuilt netloc was
  INVALID: https://[::1]:8443/x -> https://::1:8443/a — no client or
  comparator can round-trip it (urlsplit cannot parse the host back);
* different hex/compression spellings of the SAME literal produced
  different keys — [2001:DB8::1], [2001:db8::1] and the fully
  expanded [2001:0db8:0000:...:0001] were three keys for one host;
* IDN hosts were not punycoded — münchen.de and xn--mnchen-3ya.de
  were two keys for the same registrable host;
* the docstring claimed the trailing slash is PRESERVED while the code
  strips it since birth (every checkpoint id was minted with the
  strip) — docstring corrected to match the code, never the reverse.

Fix: IPv6 literals keep their brackets and are unified through
ipaddress.IPv6Address (compressed + lowercase — hex case AND
zero-compression unify); IDN hosts punycode via encode('idna') with a
verbatim fallback on malformed hosts; IPv4/domain behavior is
byte-identical with the previous contract (case folding, default-port
strip, trailing-dot strip, path/query preservation).

GREEN: 19/19 (12 contract + 7 idempotence params,
evidence/A6_green.txt). Critical wing: 696 passed / 11 skipped —
43C identity matrix, RC-5 dedup, 43C lifecycle, A1/A3/A4, and the
frozen-module gate (the file is A1-thaw-authorized; no new gate
opened, no frozen_modules.sha256 edit — delta-mode silence).
